IMPORT prelude

-- Pennsylvania Tax Reform Code of 1971 (Act of Mar. 4, 1971, P.L. 6, No. 2), Article III, Personal Income Tax -- the
-- seat-neutral core, in the Article's own terms: who is a "resident individual" (s 301(p)); the tax "upon each dollar of
-- income received" in each of the eight classes of s 303 at three and seven hundredths per cent (s 302(a), (b)); the
-- credit for income tax paid to another state (s 314); the "special tax provisions for poverty" (s 304, with ss 301(c.2),
-- (e.1), (o.2), (s.1) and s 336.1), known on the return as Tax Forgiveness; the credit for tax withheld (s 312); and the
-- duty to file a return and pay (ss 330(a), 332), written as regulative rules.
--
-- Edition: the whole Act as served by the Pennsylvania General Assembly (palegis.us) on 24 October 2026, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/pa-1971-act-2-tax-reform-code.txt; Article III is at lines 4863-7640 of the deposit.
--
-- The seat questions are in pa-pit-seat.l4, which builds on this module and restates no rule.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Tax Reform Code of 1971, Article III -- Personal Income Tax`

§§ `s 301(p) -- resident individual`

-- s 301(p): "'Resident individual' means an individual who is domiciled in this Commonwealth unless he maintains no
-- permanent place of abode in this Commonwealth and does maintain a permanent place of abode elsewhere and spends in the
-- aggregate not more than thirty days of the taxable year in this Commonwealth; or who is not domiciled in this
-- Commonwealth but maintains a permanent place of abode in this Commonwealth and spends in the aggregate more than one
-- hundred eighty-three days of the taxable year in this Commonwealth."
-- s 301(m): "'Nonresident individual' means any individual who is not a resident of the Commonwealth."
GIVEN `domiciled in this Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `maintains a permanent place of abode in this Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `maintains a permanent place of abode elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of the taxable year spent in this Commonwealth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a resident individual` IF
        (    `domiciled in this Commonwealth`
         AND (NOT (    (NOT `maintains a permanent place of abode in this Commonwealth`)
                   AND `maintains a permanent place of abode elsewhere`
                   AND `days of the taxable year spent in this Commonwealth` AT MOST 30)))
    OR  (    (NOT `domiciled in this Commonwealth`)
         AND `maintains a permanent place of abode in this Commonwealth`
         AND `days of the taxable year spent in this Commonwealth` GREATER THAN 183)

§§ `s 303 -- the classes of income`

-- s 303(a): "The classes of income referred to above are as follows: (1) Compensation. ... (2) Net profits. ... (3) Net
-- gains or income from disposition of property. ... (4) Net gains or income derived from or in the form of rents,
-- royalties, patents and copyrights. (5) Dividends. ... (6) Interest derived from obligations which are not statutorily
-- free from State or local taxation ... (7) Gambling and lottery winnings other than noncash prizes of the Pennsylvania
-- State Lottery. (8) Net gains or income derived through estates or trusts."
-- What falls into each class (the detail of s 303(a) and (a.1)-(a.12)) is taken as a fact: one amount per class, for the
-- year, as the person has worked it out. A net class may be a net loss.
DECLARE `Income by class` HAS
    `compensation`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `net profits`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `net gains or income from disposition of property`          IS A NUMBER
    `net gains or income from rents, royalties, patents and copyrights` IS A NUMBER
    `dividends`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `interest`                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `gambling and lottery winnings`                             IS A NUMBER
    `net gains or income derived through estates or trusts`     IS A NUMBER

-- s 302(a) taxes "each dollar of income received ... in each of the classes of income". Nothing in Article III lets a
-- net loss in one class reduce the income of another, so a class with a net loss contributes nothing (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the class amount taxed` n MEANS
    IF n GREATER THAN 0 THEN n ELSE 0

GIVEN i IS AN `Income by class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income taxed` i MEANS
            `the class amount taxed` (i's `compensation`)
    PLUS    `the class amount taxed` (i's `net profits`)
    PLUS    `the class amount taxed` (i's `net gains or income from disposition of property`)
    PLUS    `the class amount taxed` (i's `net gains or income from rents, royalties, patents and copyrights`)
    PLUS    `the class amount taxed` (i's `dividends`)
    PLUS    `the class amount taxed` (i's `interest`)
    PLUS    `the class amount taxed` (i's `gambling and lottery winnings`)
    PLUS    `the class amount taxed` (i's `net gains or income derived through estates or trusts`)

-- s 330(a) asks whether the taxpayer has "income for the taxable year": income in any class.
GIVEN i IS AN `Income by class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has income for the taxable year` i IF
    `the income taxed` i GREATER THAN 0

§§ `s 302 -- the tax`

-- s 302(a): every resident individual "shall pay ... a tax upon each dollar of income received by that resident during
-- that resident's taxable year at the rate of three and seven hundredths per cent." (b): every nonresident individual
-- likewise on the classes "from sources within this Commonwealth". Section 302.1 (a rate change during the year) does not
-- arise here: the deposited text states one rate.
`the rate of tax` MEANS 3.07%

-- For a nonresident, `i` is the income from sources within this Commonwealth (s 301(k)), class by class (a fact).
GIVEN i IS AN `Income by class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax imposed` i MEANS
    `the income taxed` i TIMES `the rate of tax`

§§ `s 314 -- credit for income tax paid to another state (residents only)`

-- s 314(a): "A resident taxpayer before allowance of any credit under section 312 shall be allowed a credit against the
-- tax otherwise due under this article for the amount of any income tax ... imposed on him ... by another state with
-- respect to income which is also subject to tax under this article." "State" means a state of the United States, the
-- District of Columbia, Puerto Rico and any territory or possession.
-- (b): "The credit ... shall not exceed the proportion of the tax otherwise due under this article that the amount of the
-- taxpayer's income subject to tax by the other jurisdiction bears to his entire taxable income."
GIVEN `tax otherwise due` IS A NUMBER
      `income tax paid to the other state on income also taxed here` IS A NUMBER
      `income subject to tax by the other state` IS A NUMBER
      `entire taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit for tax paid to another state` `tax otherwise due` `income tax paid to the other state on income also taxed here` `income subject to tax by the other state` `entire taxable income` MEANS
    IF `entire taxable income` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE LET `the cap` MEANS `tax otherwise due` TIMES (`income subject to tax by the other state` DIVIDED BY `entire taxable income`)
         IN IF `income tax paid to the other state on income also taxed here` LESS THAN `the cap`
            THEN `income tax paid to the other state on income also taxed here`
            ELSE `the cap`

§§ `s 304 -- special tax provisions for poverty (Tax Forgiveness)`

-- s 301(c.2): "'Claimant' means a person who is subject to the tax imposed under this article, is not a dependent of
-- another taxpayer for purposes of section 151 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 ... but is entitled to claim against
-- such tax the poverty tax provisions as provided by this act."
-- s 301(e.1): "'Dependent' means a child who is the dependent of a claimant for purposes of section 151" of the IRC
-- (a borrowed term, asked as a fact; see us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986).
-- s 301(o.2): "Poverty income" is "all moneys or property ... received of whatever nature and from whatever source
-- derived", with seven exclusions (sickness and disability payments, workers' compensation, old age or retirement
-- benefits, public assistance or unemployment compensation, reimbursed expenses, employer or union benefit programs
-- including "Social Security and retirement", combat-zone pay). Its amount is a fact.
-- s 304(d)(1): "a claimant shall not be considered to be married if: (i) The claimant and the claimant's spouse file
-- separate returns; and (ii) The claimant and the claimant's spouse live apart at all times during the last six months
-- of the taxable year or are separated pursuant to a written separation agreement."
GIVEN `married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant and spouse file separate returns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived apart at all times during the last six months of the taxable year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `separated under a written separation agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a married claimant for s 304` IF
        `married`
    AND (NOT (    `the claimant and spouse file separate returns`
              AND (   `lived apart at all times during the last six months of the taxable year`
                   OR `separated under a written separation agreement`)))

-- s 304(d)(1): "If the poverty income of the claimant during an entire taxable year is six thousand five hundred dollars
-- ($6,500) or less, or, in the case of a married claimant, if the joint poverty income of the claimant and the claimant's
-- spouse during an entire taxable year is thirteen thousand dollars ($13,000) or less, the claimant shall be entitled to
-- a refund or forgiveness of any moneys which have been paid over to (or would ... be payable to) the Commonwealth ...
-- with an additional income allowance of nine thousand five hundred dollars ($9,500) for each dependent of the claimant."
GIVEN `married claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of dependents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the poverty income limitation` `married claimant` `number of dependents` MEANS
    (IF `married claimant` THEN 13000 ELSE 6500) PLUS (9500 TIMES `number of dependents`)

-- s 304(d)(2): "If the poverty income of the claimant ... does not exceed the poverty income limitations prescribed by
-- clause (1) by more than the dollar category contained in subclauses (i) ... (ix) ... the claimant shall be entitled to
-- a refund or forgiveness based on the per centage prescribed": (i) Ninety per cent if not in excess of $250; (ii)
-- Eighty, $500; (iii) Seventy, $750; (iv) Sixty, $1,000; (v) Fifty, $1,250; (vi) Forty, $1,500; (vii) Thirty, $1,750;
-- (viii) Twenty, $2,000; (ix) Ten per cent if not in excess of $2,250.
-- `poverty income` is the joint poverty income for a married claimant.
GIVEN `poverty income` IS A NUMBER
      `married claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of dependents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share forgiven` `poverty income` `married claimant` `number of dependents` MEANS
    LET `the excess` MEANS `poverty income` MINUS (`the poverty income limitation` `married claimant` `number of dependents`)
    IN BRANCH
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 0    THEN 100%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 250  THEN 90%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 500  THEN 80%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 750  THEN 70%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 1000 THEN 60%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 1250 THEN 50%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 1500 THEN 40%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 1750 THEN 30%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 2000 THEN 20%
        IF `the excess` AT MOST 2250 THEN 10%
        OTHERWISE 0

-- Only a "claimant" can have the special tax provisions: a person subject to the tax who is not a dependent of another
-- taxpayer under IRC s 151 (s 301(c.2)). s 304(d)(3): a taxable year of less than twelve months is annualised "in such
-- manner as the department may prescribe" (not encoded: the person states a full year).
GIVEN `a dependent of another taxpayer under IRC s 151` IS A BOOLEAN
      `poverty income` IS A NUMBER
      `married claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of dependents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special tax provisions share` `a dependent of another taxpayer under IRC s 151` `poverty income` `married claimant` `number of dependents` MEANS
    IF `a dependent of another taxpayer under IRC s 151`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the share forgiven` `poverty income` `married claimant` `number of dependents`

§§ `ss 312, 314, 304 -- what is left to pay`

-- The order: s 314(a) is allowed "before allowance of any credit under section 312"; s 304 forgives a share of "any moneys
-- which have been paid over to (or would ... be payable to) the Commonwealth under ... this article", read here as the
-- tax after the s 314 credit (NOTES.md finding 4); s 312: "The amount withheld ... shall be allowed ... as a credit
-- against the tax". A negative result is an overpayment, refunded or credited under s 346 (not encoded).
GIVEN `tax imposed` IS A NUMBER
      `credit for tax paid to another state` IS A NUMBER
      `share forgiven` IS A NUMBER
      `tax withheld and estimated tax paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the balance due` `tax imposed` `credit for tax paid to another state` `share forgiven` `tax withheld and estimated tax paid` MEANS
    LET `the liability` MEANS `tax imposed` MINUS `credit for tax paid to another state`
    IN (`the liability` MINUS (`the liability` TIMES `share forgiven`)) MINUS `tax withheld and estimated tax paid`

§§ `ss 330, 332, 336.1 -- the return, the payment and the claim (regulative)`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the claimant`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `file a Pennsylvania personal income tax return`
    `pay the tax due`
    `claim the special tax provisions with the annual return`

-- s 330(a): "On or before the date when the taxpayer's Federal income tax return is due or would be due if the taxpayer
-- were required to file a Federal income tax return ... a tax return under this article shall be made and filed by or
-- for every taxpayer having income for the taxable year."
-- s 332: "A person required to make and file a return under this article shall, without assessment, notice or demand,
-- pay any tax due thereon to the department on or before the date fixed for filing such return (determined without
-- regard to any extension of time for filing the return)."
-- Days are counted from the end of the taxable year; the federal due date is a fact (IRC s 6072, not deposited), so the
-- number of days to it is an input. An extension of time to file (s 334) is the department's and is not encoded; it does
-- not move the day for payment.
GIVEN `days to the federal return due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to file a return` `days to the federal return due date` MEANS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    MUST  `file a Pennsylvania personal income tax return`
    WITHIN `days to the federal return due date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "a taxpayer having income for the taxable year did not file the return s 330(a) requires by the federal return due date"

GIVEN `days to the federal return due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to pay the tax due` `days to the federal return due date` MEANS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    MUST  `pay the tax due`
    WITHIN `days to the federal return due date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "the tax due was not paid by the date fixed for filing the return (s 332), whatever extension of time to file was granted"

-- s 336.1(1): "The claimant may claim the special tax provisions upon the expiration of his taxable year in connection
-- with his filing of an annual return under the provisions of this article." A permission: not claiming is no breach.
GIVEN `days to the federal return due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the permission to claim the special tax provisions` `days to the federal return due date` MEANS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MAY   `claim the special tax provisions with the annual return`
    WITHIN `days to the federal return due date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
